<title>INDIA: HSBC CAPITAL GETS INDIA MERCHANT BANKING LICENCE.</title>
<headline>HSBC CAPITAL GETS INDIA MERCHANT BANKING LICENCE.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC Capital Markets India Pvt Ltd on Monday said it received a Category I merchant banking licence from the Securities and Exchange Board of Inda (SEBI).</p>
<p>HSBC Investment Banking, part of the HSBC Group has over 5,000 offices and assets of $458 billion at end June 1997, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91)-22-265 9000</p>
